{{Quote|Your species is smarter than you appear.|[[Lok Durd]] to [[Tee Watt Kaa]], the leader of a colony of [[Lurmen]]|<ref name="DoP">{{TCW|Defenders of Peace}}</ref>}}
[[File:Cantinapuzzle.png|thumb|right|300px|A group of various species in a cantina]]
A '''species''' was a group of living '''organisms''' that shared a fixed set of observable biological characteristics. [[The galaxy]] and its many [[planet]]s were teeming with diverse species. Some species were [[sentience|sentient]], capable of intelligent thinking, while others were not,<ref name="Vandor">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story: Tales from Vandor]]''</ref> with more than twenty million sentient species in the [[galaxy]].<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|starwars|status/1531519656254590976|Star Wars|quote=There are more than 20 million sentient species in the Star Wars galaxy, don't choose to be a racist.|archivedate=20220531190530}}</ref> The majority of known species, both sentient and non-sentient, exhibited a [[carbon]]-[[Carbon-based life form|based]] biochemistry. However, a smaller subset of life forms possessed alternative biochemical structures, including [[silicon]]-[[Silicon-based organism|based]],<ref name="BMF 43">{{BuildFalconCite|43|Secrets of Spaceflight}}</ref> and [[Mercury|mercury]]-based biochemistries.<ref name="Sanctuary">''[[Sanctuary: A Bad Batch Novel]]''</ref> All species organisms eventually [[death|died]], though through the process of [[reproduction]], new [[Youngling|life]] was created to carry a species on another generation.<ref name="Leia, Princess of Alderaan">''[[Leia, Princess of Alderaan]]''</ref> Some species had subspecies, which was group of organisms a species capable of interbreeding with similar organisms, though had traits that were distinct to some traits in other members of the species.<ref name="Bestiary">''[[Star Wars Bestiary, Vol. 1: Creatures of the Galaxy]]''</ref>

==Types of species==

===Microorganisms===
Many types of microorganisms existed, including [[Fungus|fungi]], [[Virus (disambiguation)|viruses]], and [[bacteria]], each having their own set of species. Many species of viruses and bacteria had ability to [[disease|infect other species]], such as the [[death|deadly]] [[Blue Shadow Virus]].<ref name="Blue Shadow Virus">{{TCW|Blue Shadow Virus (episode)}}</ref> While most species of fungus did not possess [[sentience]], some appeared to show signs of emerging sentience<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> or were eaten by other creatures.<ref name="NoP">''[[Nexus of Power]]''</ref>

===Plants===
{{Main|Plant}}
[[File:Mina-Rau_Agricultural_Silo.png|thumb|left|200px|[[Wheat]], a species of [[plant]], was grown on the planet [[Mina-Rau]] for use in food]]
{{Quote|That's the trouble with plants... Pull them up or cut them down, all they need is one tiny ssscrap in the darkness... A ssseed or a root... Hidden away, out of sssight. Out of mind. They grow back, ssstronger than before. Indomitable. Unyielding.|[[Sskeer]], to [[Keeve Trennis]]|<ref name="High5">[[The High Republic (2021) 5|''The High Republic'' (2021) 5]]</ref>}}
Many types of plants species, including [[tree]]s, herbs, [[bush]]es, [[grass]]es, vines, [[Fern (plant)|fern]]s, [[moss]]es, and [[Color|green]] [[algae]],<ref name="RoS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref>  which generally<ref name="Occlusion Zone 4">[[The High Republic Adventures – Dispatches from the Occlusion Zone 4|''The High Republic Adventures – Dispatches from the Occlusion Zone'' 4]]</ref> fed of [[Star|sunlight]],<ref name="RoS VD" /> and [[Reproduction|reproduced]] by sprouting seeds that would develop into new plants.<ref name="Uprooted">{{YJA|Uprooted}}</ref> Different species of plants were used for various purposes by sentient beings, such as being used in [[foodstuff]]s<ref name="Galactic Bake-Off">''[[The High Republic Adventures: Galactic Bake-Off Spectacular]]''</ref> or for medicinal properties.<ref name="MoTM">{{TCW|Mystery of a Thousand Moons}}</ref>

===Creatures===
Creatures was a collective term to describe all lifeforms with sentience. All creatures required energy to sustain themselves, often though the consumption of [[foodstuff]], liquids, and or [[gas|gasses]] such as [[oxygen]] to sustain itself, with different species having their own [[diet|diets]]. Many creatures required [[sleep]].<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref> Many lifeforms were categorized by unique features, such as the [[Mon Calamari]], who were categorized as an [[Amphibian|amphibious]] species.<ref name="Worldwide 217">{{InsiderCite|217|Worldwide}}</ref> 

====Beasts====
[[File:Rancor-SWE.png||thumb|right|150px|[[Rancor]]s were a species of beast with emerging intelligence]]
Beasts,<ref name="sweRUP">{{SWE|characters|ruping|ruping}}</ref><ref name="sweNEX">{{SWE|characters|nexu|nexu}}</ref> also known as animals,<ref name="Convert">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 19: The Convert}}</ref> were creatures with a limited or lack of [[sentience]]. Beasts came in many different species, ranging from small to large in both shape and size, from the small [[Nuna]]s from [[Naboo]]<ref name="databank">{{Databank|nuna|Nuna}}</ref> to the towering [[Zillo Beast]]s of [[Malastare]].<ref name="ZilloDatabank">{{Databank|zillo-beast|Zillo Beast}}</ref> Many beasts were categorized in animal types such as [[Bird]]s, [[Fish]], [[Spider]]s, [[Dog]]s, and [[Insect]]s. Many other animals, such as [[Rathtar]]s, did not fall into a category, and simply were known by their similarity to other species,<ref name="TFA VD">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> or were simply known by a distinctive features like similar to other creatures, such as [[Rancor]]s, who were classified as being reptilian.<ref name="sweRAN">{{SWE|characters|rancor|rancor}}</ref>

[[File:NerfHerder-AaA.png||thumb|left|150px|a [[human]] [[Nerf herder]] watching over their herd of [[Nerf]]s]]
Many species of beasts were grown, caught, or harvested for their byproducts or organic matter by species with higher intelligence for consumption or use in products. For example, the [[Nerf]] species were often grown to be harvested for their [[milk]], meat,<ref name="cookbook">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge: The Official Black Spire Outpost Cookbook]]''</ref> or [[Nerf-hide]].<ref name="TFA VD">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> As such, some professions held my fully sentient species, such as [[fisher|fishermen]]<ref name="Traveler's Guide">''[[Star Wars: Galaxy's Edge: Traveler's Guide to Batuu]]''</ref> or [[Nerf herder]]s were made around the harvesting of an animal species.<ref name="Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref> The fully sentient populations of some [[planet]]s relied on the harvesting of animal byproducts, such as the [[Ghorman (people)|people]] of the planet [[Ghorman]], who's economy relied on the production of [[Ghorman twill]], a fabric made from a [[Ghorman silk|silk]] produced by a species of spider known as [[Ghorlectipod]]s.<ref name="GhormanSpiderDB">{{Databank|ghorman-spider|Ghorman spider}}</ref>

====Sentients====
{{Main|Alien}}
{{Quote|Sentients, please prepare for takeoff!|Pilot droid [[R-3X|RX-24]] addresses his passengers|<ref name="Droids in Distress">{{Rebels|Droids in Distress}}</ref>}}
[[File:The_Quarren.png||thumb|right|200px|The [[Quarren]] were a sentient species from the planet [[Mon Cala|Dac]]]]
Sentients were fully [[Sentience|sentient]] creatures that possessed the ability to communicate with others. Sentients ranged in size and shape, from the short and nimble [[Anzellan]]s<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> from [[Anzell system|Anzell]]<ref name="Planetnamia">{{Planetnamia|species=Anzellan|homeworld=[[Anzell system|Anzell]]}}</ref> to the large [[slug]]-like<ref name="Episode"RoTJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref> [[Hutt]]s from [[Nal Hutta]].<ref name="Nal Hutta">{{Databank|nal-hutta|Nal Hutta}}</ref> Many other species that structurally resembled humans were referred to as "[[humanoid]]s."<ref name="EncyclopediaZy">{{SWE|groups|zygerrians|Zygerrians}}</ref> Members of unique sentient species often took advantage (or were taken advantage) of their unique biology to complete different tasks, and also often had their own cultures and traditions, sometimes including their own [[language]]s.<ref name="Episode"RoTJ" /> For example, the [[Wookiee]]s of the planet [[Kashyyyk]]<ref name="AbEverything">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> observed the [[holiday]] known as [[Life Day]],<ref name="LifeDayDatabank">{{Databank|life-day|Life Day}}</ref> and spoke the unique languages of [[Shyriiwook]],<ref name="AbEverything" /> [[Thykarann]],<ref name="AbEverything" /> and [[Xaczik]].<ref name="AbEverything" /> The largest group of sentient species were [[Human]]s, who constituted a plurality of [[the galaxy]]'s inhabitants. As a result, [[Xenophobia]] towards '[[alien]]s', a term used by humans to describe non-humans,<ref name="whatwookiee">[[Star Wars: What is a Wookiee? (2015)|''What is a Wookiee?'']]</ref> became increasingly common that by the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], a policy of [[High Human|human-centrism]] was adopted.<ref name="TROS VD" />

